        "id": 51897,
        "name": "pwatson1974",
        "username": "pwatson1974",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/pwatson1974/{size}/1925_2.png",
        "created_at": "2013-01-10T20:11:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>1st question is currently causing a philosophical discussion in the \"Can't deal damage thread\". Personally, I rule that even if you're immune to the damage, you can still take it. Otherwise, Ra would have to destroy ongouings to deal with a Fire in the Biosphere, which really doesn't match my conception of how Ra should handle fire.</p><p>2nd, it's per hero. The \"belonging to THAT hero\" is the part that specifies that this is a per hero effect, versus Baron Blade's Devious Disruption which affects everyone.</p>",
        "post_number": 2,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T02:25:39.053Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
